# Normalise text in the repository, and check it out with LF where the tool
# that reads it cares. The build runs inside a Linux container even on
# Windows hosts: a shell script or Makefile checked out with CRLF fails there
# in ways that read as anything but a line-ending problem.
* text=auto

*.sh    text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.c     text eol=lf
*.h     text eol=lf
*.C     text eol=lf
*.H     text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# Never touched: the game's config parser terminates lines on CR and walks off
# the end of its buffer without one. Nothing here is committed today (it is
# staged from your own copy of the game), but if that ever changes, it must
# not be normalised.
*.cfg   -text
*.CFG   -text
